 "result_text": "I fixed the MQTT publish so `$ext` functions in a `json` block are now evaluated. I haven't run any tests or tried it against a real publish.\n\nThe old code called `update_from_ext` on `publish_args` after `json` had already been turned into a string. At that point `json` no longer existed, so the `$ext` block was never seen. In `tavern/_plugins/mqtt/request.py`, I moved the call into `get_publish_args`. It now runs on the `json` dict just before that dict is dumped to the `payload` string. I removed the old call in `MQTTRequest.__init__`.\n\nYour request config looks correct, and I made no change to the config format. The function's return value is merged into the `json` body, as with other `$ext` uses. In your example the published payload should be `thing_1: abc` plus whatever `my_function` returns.\n\nI didn't change the `payload` key. It's still a plain string, so `$ext` only works under `json`, not `payload`.",
